","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"TreeRestoreSpan carries a tree node run from a single deletion, addressed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by TreeNodeID identity, for identity-preserving Tree undo\/redo. Unlike the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text RestoreSpan (flat offsets), a tree span records the node’s structure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(type\/attrs) and its position anchors, because in a tree id-order is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sibling-order: left_sibling_id and right_sibling_id are redundant external"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary anchors of the deleted run, so restore can reconstruct the run’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal order from the op’s own spans and needs only one surviving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary to place it. value\/attributes are a deep copy so a GC-purged node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be recreated."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan/init(serializedBytes:extensions:partial:options:)-7lhws":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/init(serializedBytes:extensions:partial:options:)-7lhws","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Bytes"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"serializedBytes"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bytes"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"extensions","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExtensionMap","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdent